SSL_open_app_data is the read-side counterpart of SSL_seal_app_data: it
opens one record in place in the caller's buffer through the same
ssl_open_app_data path SSL_read uses, then processes any post-handshake
message the record completed. Every other state is left to SSL_read,
which also reports a close_notify or error met here.

The bssl_shim flag -open-app-data reads through it. A filter BIO holds
the input the shim pulled ahead of BoringSSL, so SSL_read continues
where opening stops, and the runner suite passes with the flag.
